    "notes": "Targets were z-scored in training (normalize: true) and the training mean/SD are not shipped; the inverse uses the paper's Table 1 cohort values (3.99 +/- 0.50 mmol/L), so absolute calibration is approximate and MAE/bias carry that error; rank-based metrics do not. The paper's median model is #3; the card averages all five. Elliptic 0.8 Hz high-pass (authors' remove_baseline_filter) runs in the wrapper on the unpadded 10 s. MIT / CC-BY."
